        "right": "op + 1"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_overflow_sink_write_exceeds_output_slice",
      "fine_trace_step": 15,
      "description": "ASAN crash site. The leftover-literal path writes one more byte through `op` after the inflated `op_limit` failed to stop the encoder, so the byte store lands just past the heap allocation returned by `malloc(size + 1)` in the harness."
    },
